{
  "title": "43: al-Zukhruf الزخرف",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nحٰمٓ ‌ ۛ‌ۚ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa-Mim \nوَالْكِتٰبِ الْمُبِيْنِ ‌ ۛ‌ۙ‏(2)\nWAL KETAABE MOBEEN.\nBy the Book that makes things clear, \nاِنَّا جَعَلْنٰهُ قُرْءٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(3)\nINNAA LAW QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL LA-A’LLAKUM TA’QELOON.\nWe have made it a Qur'an in Arabic, that ye may be able to understand (and learn wisdom). \nوَاِنَّهٗ فِىْۤ اُمِّ الْكِتٰبِ لَدَيْنَا لَعَلِىٌّ حَكِيْمٌؕ‏(4)\nWA INNAHU FEE UMME KETAABE LADAYNAA LAA’ALEAAAUN HAKEEMUN.\nAnd verily, it is in the Mother of the Book, in Our Presence, high (in dignity), full of wisdom. \nاَفَنَضْرِبُ عَنْكُمُ الذِّكْرَ صَفْحًا اَنْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا مُّسْرِفِيْنَ‏(5)\nAAFANAZREBU LEYUZHEBA KHASEYAR SAFHAN AN KUNTUM QAWMAN MMUSREFEENA.\nShall We then take away the Message from you and repel (you), for that ye are a people transgressing beyond bounds? \nوَكَمْ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ نَّبِىٍّ فِى الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(6)\nWA ARSALNAA MIN NNABEAAAIN FIL AWWALEEN.\nBut how many were the prophets We sent amongst the peoples of old? \nوَمَا يَاْتِيْهِمْ مِّنْ نَّبِىٍّ اِلَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(7)\nWA MAA YAATEEHIM MIN NNABEAAAIN ILLAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nAnd never came there a prophet to them but they mocked him. \nفَاَهْلَكْنَاۤ اَشَدَّ مِنْهُمْ بَطْشًا وَّمَضٰى مَثَلُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(8)\nFA AHLAKNAL ASHADDA MINHUM BATSHAN WWAMAZAA MASALUL AWWALEEN.\nSo We destroyed (them)- stronger in power than these;- and (thus) has passed on the Parable of the peoples of old. \nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ خَلَقَهُنَّ الْعَزِيْزُ الْعَلِيْمُۙ‏(9)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM MAN KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA LAYAQOOLUNNAL KHALAQAHUNNA A’ZEEZUL A’LEEM.\nIf thou wert to question them, 'Who created the heavens and the earth?' They would be sure to reply, 'they were created by (Him), the Exalted in Power, Full of Knowledge';- \nالَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ مَهْدًا وَّ جَعَلَ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا سُبُلًا لَّعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(10)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA MAHDAN WA JA-A’LA LAKUM FEEHAA SUBULAN LA-A’LLAKUM TAHTADOON.\n(Yea, the same that) has made for you the earth (like a carpet) spread out, and has made for you roads (and channels) therein, in order that ye may find guidance (on the way); \nوَالَّذِىْ نَزَّلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءًۢ بِقَدَرٍ‌ۚ فَاَنْشَرْنَا بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا‌ ۚ كَذٰلِكَ تُخْرَجُوْنَ‏(11)\nWAL LAZEE NAZZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN BEQADARIN FAANSHARNAA BEHI BALDATAN MMAYTAN KAZAALEKA TUKHRAJOON.\nThat sends down (from time to time) rain from the sky in due measure;- and We raise to life therewith a land that is dead; even so will ye be raised (from the dead);- \nوَالَّذِىْ خَلَقَ الْاَزْوَاجَ كُلَّهَا وَجَعَلَ لَكُمْ مِّنَ الْفُلْكِ وَالْاَنْعَامِ مَا تَرْكَبُوْنَۙ‏(12)\nWAL LAZEE KHALAQAL AZWAAJA KULLAHAA WA LAKUM MENAL FULKE WAL AANA’AAME MAA TARKABOONA.\nThat has created pairs in all things, and has made for you ships and cattle on which ye ride, \nلِتَسْتَوٗا عَلٰى ظُهُوْرِهٖ ثُمَّ تَذْكُرُوْا نِعْمَةَ رَبِّكُمْ اِذَا اسْتَوَيْتُمْ عَلَيْهِ وَتَقُوْلُوْا سُبْحٰنَ الَّذِىْ سَخَّرَ لَنَا هٰذَا وَمَا كُنَّا لَهٗ مُقْرِنِيْنَۙ‏(13)\nLETASTAWA A’LAA ZUHOOREH SUMMA TAZKUROOA NE’MATAL RABBEKUM EZAA ASTAWAYTUM A’LAYHE WA TAQOOLOO LAAHE LAZEE SAKKHARA LANAA HAAZAA WA MAA KUNNAA LAHU MUQRENEENA.\nIn order that ye may sit firm and square on their backs, and when so seated, ye may celebrate the (kind) favour of your Lord, and say, “Glory to Him Who has subjected these to our (use), for we could never have accomplished this (by ourselves), \nوَاِنَّاۤ اِلٰى رَبِّنَا لَمُنْقَلِبُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA INNAA ELAA RABBENAA LAMUNQALEBOONA.\n“And to our Lord, surely, must we turn back!” \nوَجَعَلُوْا لَهٗ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ جُزْءًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لَكَفُوْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ ؕ‏(15)\nWA JA-A’LOO LAHU MIN E’BAADEHI JUZ-AN INNAL INSAANA LAKAFOORUN MOBEEN.\nYet they attribute to some of His servants a share with Him (in his godhead)! truly is man a blasphemous ingrate avowed! \nاَمِ اتَّخَذَ مِمَّا يَخْلُقُ بَنٰتٍ وَّاَصْفٰٮكُمْ بِالْبَنِيْنَ‏(16)\nAMIL TAKHAZA MIMMAA YAKHLOQO BANAATIN WWAASFAAKUM BIL-BANEENA.\nWhat! has He taken daughters out of what He himself creates, and granted to you sons for choice? \nوَاِذَا بُشِّرَ اَحَدُهُمْ بِمَا ضَرَبَ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ مَثَلًا ظَلَّ وَجْهُهٗ مُسْوَدًّا وَّهُوَ كَظِيْمٌ‏(17)\nWA EZAA BUSSHERA AHADOHUM BEMAA ZARABA LELRRAHMAANE MASALAA ZALLA WAJHUH MUSWADDAN WA KAZEEMUN.\nWhen news is brought to one of them of (the birth of) what he sets up as a likeness to (Allah) Most Gracious, his face darkens, and he is filled with inward grief! \nاَوَمَنْ يُّنَشَّؤُا فِى الْحِلْيَةِ وَهُوَ فِى الْخِصَامِ غَيْرُ مُبِيْنٍ‏(18)\nAAWAMAN YYUNASSHAUA FIL AL-HELYATE WA HOWA FIL KHESAAM GHAYRO MUBEENIN.\nIs then one brought up among trinkets, and unable to give a clear account in a dispute (to be associated with Allah)? \nوَجَعَلُوا الْمَلٰٓئِكَةَ الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عِبَادُ الرَّحْمٰنِ اِنَاثًا‌ ؕ اَشَهِدُوْا خَلْقَهُمْ‌ ؕ سَتُكْتَبُ شَهَادَتُهُمْ وَيُسْئَلُوْنَ‏(19)\nWAJAA’ALOOA AL-MALAAAEKATA LAZEENA HUM E’EBAADU RAHMAANIR AENAASAN AASHAHEDOOA KHALQAHUM SATUKTABU SHAHAADATUHUM WAYUSALOONA.\nAnd they make into females angels who themselves serve Allah. Did they witness their creation? Their evidence will be recorded, and they will be called to account! \nوَقَالُوْا لَوْ شَآءَ الرَّحْمٰنُ مَا عَبَدْنٰهُمْ‌ؕ مَا لَهُمْ بِذٰلِكَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَخْرُصُوْنَؕ‏(20)\nWA QAALOO LAW SHAAA-AL RAHMAANO MAA A’ABADNAAHUM MAA LAHUM BE-ZAALEKA MIN I’LMIN IN HUM ILLAA YAKHRUSOONA.\n(“Ah!”) they say, “If it had been the will of (Allah) Most Gracious, we should not have worshipped such (deities)!” Of that they have no knowledge! they do nothing but lie! \nاَمْ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ كِتٰبًا مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ فَهُمْ بِهٖ مُسْتَمْسِكُوْنَ‏(21)\nAM AATAYNAAHUM KETAABAA MIN QABLEHI FAHUM BEHI MUSTAMSEKOONA.\nWhat! have We given them a Book before this, to which they are holding fast? \nبَلْ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا عَلٰٓى اُمَّةٍ وَّاِنَّا عَلٰٓى اٰثٰرِهِمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(22)\nBAL QAALOO INNAA WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA A’LAA UMMATIN WWAANNAA A’LAA AAASAAREHEM HUM MOHTADOON.\nNay! they say: “We found our fathers following a certain religion, and we do guide ourselves by their footsteps.” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ مَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ فِىْ قَرْيَةٍ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ اِلَّا قَالَ مُتْرَفُوْهَاۤ اِنَّا وَجَدْنَاۤ اٰبَآءَنَا عَلٰٓى اُمَّةٍ وَّاِنَّا عَلٰٓى اٰثٰرِهِمْ مُّقْتَدُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA KAZAALEKA MAA ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA FEE QARYATINW MIN NAZEERIM ILLAA QAALA MUTRAFOOHAA INNAA WAJADNAA AABAAA-ANAA A’LAA UMMATIN WWAANNAA A’LAA AAASAAREHEM MMUQTADOONA.\nJust in the same way, whenever We sent a Warner before thee to any people, the wealthy ones among them said: “We found our fathers following a certain religion, and we will certainly follow in their footsteps.” \nقٰلَ اَوَلَوْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِاَهْدٰى مِمَّا وَجَدْتُّمْ عَلَيْهِ اٰبَآءَكُمْ‌ ؕ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلْتُمْ بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(24)\nQAALA LAW JETUKUM BE-AHDAA MIMMAA WAJADTTUM A’LAYHE AABAAA-AKUM QAALOO INNAA BEMAA URSILTUM BEHI KAAFEROON.\nHe said: “What! Even if I brought you better guidance than that which ye found your fathers following?” They said: “For us, we deny that ye (prophets) are sent (on a mission at all).” \nفَانْتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْ‌ فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُكَذِّبِيْنَ‏(25)\nFAN-TAQAMNAA MINHUM FANZUR KAYFA KAANA A’AQEBATUL MOKAZZEBEENAZ.\nSo We exacted retribution from them: now see what was the end of those who rejected (Truth)! \nوَاِذْ قَالَ اِبْرٰهِيْمُ لِاَبِيْهِ وَقَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّنِىْ بَرَآءٌ مِّمَّا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(26)\nWA IZ QAALA AEBRAAHEEMU LEAABEEHE WA QAWMEHI INNANEE BARAAUN MIMMAA TA’BODOONA.\nBehold! Abraham said to his father and his people: “I do indeed clear myself of what ye worship: \nاِلَّا الَّذِىْ فَطَرَنِىْ فَاِنَّهٗ سَيَهْدِيْنِ‏(27)\nILLAA LAZEE FATARANEE FA-INNAHU SAYAHDEENE.\n“(I worship) only Him Who made me, and He will certainly guide me.” \nوَ جَعَلَهَا كَلِمَةًۢ بَاقِيَةً فِىْ عَقِبِهٖ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA JAA’ALAHAA KALEMATAN BAAQEETAN FEE A’AQEBEH LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nAnd he left it as a Word to endure among those who came after him, that they may turn back (to Allah). \nبَلْ مَتَّعْتُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ وَاٰبَآءَهُمْ حَتّٰى جَآءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ وَرَسُوْلٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(29)\nBAL MATTAA’TU HAAOOLAAA-E WA AA-BAAA-AHUM HATTAA JAAA-AHOMUL HAQQO WA RASOOLUM MOBEEN.\nYea, I have given the good things of this life to these (men) and their fathers, until the Truth has come to them, and a messenger making things clear. \nوَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمُ الْحَقُّ قَالُوْا هٰذَا سِحْرٌ وَّاِنَّا بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AHOMUL HAQQO QAALOO HAAZAA SEHRUM WWAANNAA BEHI KAAFEROON.\nBut when the Truth came to them, they said: “This is sorcery, and we do reject it.” \nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَا نُزِّلَ هٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنُ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ مِّنَ الْقَرْيَتَيْنِ عَظِيْمٍ‏(31)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA NUZZELA HAAZAA QUR-AANO A’LAA RAJULIN MENAL AL-QARYATAYNE A’ZEEM.\nAlso, they say: “Why is not this Qur'an sent down to some leading man in either of the two (chief) cities?” \nاَهُمْ يَقْسِمُوْنَ رَحْمَتَ رَبِّكَ‌ ؕ نَحْنُ قَسَمْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ مَّعِيْشَتَهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا وَرَفَعْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ فَوْقَ بَعْضٍ دَرَجٰتٍ لِّيَتَّخِذَ بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا سُخْرِيًّا‌ ؕ وَرَحْمَتُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ مِّمَّا يَجْمَعُوْنَ‏(32)\nA HUM YAQSEMOONA RAHMATAL RABBEKA NAHNO QASAMNAA BAYNAHUM MMAE’EESHATAHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA WA RAFA’NAA BA’ZAHUM FAWQA ELAA DARAJAATIN LLEETTAKHEZA KHALAA BA’ZAN SUKHREEA WARAHMATU RABBEKA KHAYRUL MIMMAA YAJMAU’OONA.\nIs it they who would portion out the Mercy of thy Lord? It is We Who portion out between them their livelihood in the life of this world: and We raise some of them above others in ranks, so that some may command work from others. But the Mercy of thy Lord is better than the (wealth) which they amass. \nوَلَوْلَاۤ اَنْ يَّكُوْنَ النَّاسُ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً لَّجَعَلْنَا لِمَنْ يَّكْفُرُ بِالرَّحْمٰنِ لِبُيُوْتِهِمْ سُقُفًا مِّنْ فِضَّةٍ وَّمَعَارِجَ عَلَيْهَا يَظْهَرُوْنَۙ‏(33)\nWA LAWLAA AN YAKOONA NAASO UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN LLAJAA’ALNAA LEMAN-Y YYAKFURU BE-RAHMAANIR LEBUYOOTEHEM SUQUFAN MIN FIZZATIWN WWAMAA’AAREJA A’LAYHAA YAZHAROONA.\nAnd were it not that (all) men might become of one (evil) way of life, We would provide, for everyone that blasphemes against (Allah) Most Gracious, silver roofs for their houses and (silver) stair-ways on which to go up, \nوَلِبُيُوْتِهِمْ اَبْوَابًا وَّسُرُرًا عَلَيْهَا يَتَّكِئُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nWALEBUYOOTEHEM ABWAABANW WWASURURAN A’LAYHAA YATTAKEOONA.\nAnd (silver) doors to their houses, and thrones (of silver) on which they could recline, \nوَزُخْرُفًا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ كُلُّ ذٰ لِكَ لَمَّا مَتَاعُ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا‌ ؕ وَالْاٰخِرَةُ عِنْدَ رَبِّكَ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(35)\nWAZUKHRUFAN WA KULLO ZAA LEKA LAMMAA MATAAU’U HAYAATID DUNYAA WAL AAKHERATO I’NDAL RABBEKA LILMUTTAQEEN.\nAnd also adornments of gold. But all this were nothing but conveniences of the present life: The Hereafter, in the sight of thy Lord is for the Righteous. \nوَمَنْ يَّعْشُ عَنْ ذِكْرِ الرَّحْمٰنِ نُقَيِّضْ لَهٗ شَيْطٰنًا فَهُوَ لَهٗ قَرِيْنٌ‏(36)\nWA MAN YYAA’SHU A’N ELAA RAHMAANIR NUQAYZ LAHU SHAYTAANAN FAHOWA LAHU QAREENUN.\nIf anyone withdraws himself from remembrance of (Allah) Most Gracious, We appoint for him an evil one, to be an intimate companion to him. \nوَاِنَّهُمْ لَيَصُدُّوْنَهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ وَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّهُمْ مُّهْتَدُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA INNAHUM LAYASUDDOONAHUM A’NIL SABEELE WA YAHSABOONAL ANNAHUM HUM MOHTADOON.\nSuch (evil ones) really hinder them from the Path, but they think that they are being guided aright! \nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَنَا قَالَ يٰلَيْتَ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكَ بُعْدَ الْمَشْرِقَيْنِ فَبِئْسَ الْقَرِيْنُ‏(38)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-ANAA QAALA YAALAYTA BAYNEE WA WA BUA’DA MASHREQAYNE FA MASALUL AL-QAREENU.\nAt length, when (such a one) comes to Us, he says (to his evil companion): “Would that between me and thee were the distance of East and West!” Ah! evil is the companion (indeed)! \nوَلَنْ يَّنْفَعَكُمُ الْيَوْمَ اِذْ ظَّلَمْتُمْ اَنَّكُمْ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُشْتَرِكُوْنَ‏(39)\nWA LAN YANFA-A’KOMUL YAWMA IZ ZZALAMTUM ANNAKUM FIL A’ZAABE MUSHTAREKOONA.\nWhen ye have done wrong, it will avail you nothing, that Day, that ye shall be partners in Punishment! \nاَفَاَنْتَ تُسْمِعُ الصُّمَّ اَوْ تَهْدِى الْعُمْىَ وَمَنْ كَانَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(40)\nAAFAANTA TUSME-U’S SUMMAD AW TAHDEAA AL-U’UMAAA WA MAN KAANA FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nCanst thou then make the deaf to hear, or give direction to the blind or to such as (wander) in manifest error? \nفَاِمَّا نَذْهَبَنَّ بِكَ فَاِنَّا مِنْهُمْ مُّنْتَقِمُوْنَۙ‏(41)\nFA-IMMAA NAZHABANNA BEKA FAINNAA MINHUM MMUNTAQEMOONA.\nEven if We take thee away, We shall be sure to exact retribution from them, \nاَوْ نُرِيَنَّكَ الَّذِىْ وَعَدْنٰهُمْ فَاِنَّا عَلَيْهِمْ مُّقْتَدِرُوْنَ‏(42)\nAW NUREENNAKA LAZEE WAA’ADNAAHUM FAINNAA A’LAYHIM MMUQTADEROONA.\nOr We shall show thee that (accomplished) which We have promised them: for verily We shall prevail over them. \nفَاسْتَمْسِكْ بِالَّذِىْۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ‌ ۚ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(43)\nFAASTAMSEK BIL-LAZEE OOHEYA ELAYKA INNAKA A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nSo hold thou fast to the Revelation sent down to thee; verily thou art on a Straight Way. \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَذِكْرٌ لَّكَ وَلِقَوْمِكَ‌ ۚ وَسَوْفَ تُسْئَلُوْنَ‏(44)\nWA INNAHU LAZEKRUN LAKA WALEQAWMEKA WA SAWFA TUS-ALOONA.\nThe (Qur'an) is indeed the message, for thee and for thy people; and soon shall ye (all) be brought to account. \nوَسْئَلْ مَنْ اَرْسَلْنَا مِنْ قَبْلِكَ مِنْ رُّسُلِنَاۤ اَجَعَلْنَا مِنْ دُوْنِ الرَّحْمٰنِ اٰلِهَةً يُّعْبَدُوْنَ‏(45)\nWASAL MAN ARSALNAA MIN QABLEKA MIN RRUSULENAA AAJAA’ALNAA MIN DOONIL RAHMAANIR AALEHATAL YYUA’BADOONA.\nAnd question thou our messengers whom We sent before thee; did We appoint any deities other than (Allah) Most Gracious, to be worshipped? \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۫ئِه فَقَالَ اِنِّىْ رَسُوْلُ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA ELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAAEH FAQAALA INNEE RASOOLAL RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nWe did send Moses aforetime, with Our Signs, to Pharaoh and his Chiefs: He said, “I am a messenger of the Lord of the Worlds.” \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِذَا هُمْ مِّنْهَا يَضْحَكُوْنَ‏(47)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-AHUM BE-AAYAATENAA EZAA HUM MINHAA YAZHAKOON.\nBut when he came to them with Our Signs, behold they ridiculed them. \nوَمَا نُرِيْهِمْ مِّنْ اٰيَةٍ اِلَّا هِىَ اَكْبَرُ مِنْ اُخْتِهَا‌ وَ اَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِالْعَذَابِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَرْجِعُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA MAA NUREEHEM MIN AAYATIM ILLAA HEYA AKBARO MIN AUKHTEHAA WA AAKHAZNAAHUM BE-A’ZAABE LA-A’LLAHUM YARJE-O’ON.\nWe showed them Sign after Sign, each greater than its fellow, and We seized them with Punishment, in order that they might turn (to Us). \nوَقَالُوْا يٰۤاَيُّهَ السَّاحِرُ ادْعُ لَنَا رَبَّكَ بِمَا عَهِدَ عِنْدَكَ‌ۚ اِنَّنَا لَمُهْتَدُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA QAALOO YAA AYYOHAS AS-SAAHERU O’ LANAA RABBAKA BEMAA A’AHEDA E’ENDAKA INNANAA LA-MOHTADOON.\nAnd they said, “O thou sorcerer! Invoke thy Lord for us according to His covenant with thee; for we shall truly accept guidance.” \nفَلَمَّا كَشَفْنَا عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابَ اِذَا هُمْ يَنْكُثُوْنَ‏(50)\nFALAMMAA KASHAFNAA A’NHOMUL A’ZAABA EZAA HUM YANKUSOONA.\nBut when We removed the Penalty from them, behold, they broke their word. \nوَنَادٰى فِرْعَوْنُ فِىْ قَوْمِهٖ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَلَيْسَ لِىْ مُلْكُ مِصْرَ وَهٰذِهِ الْاَنْهٰرُ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِىْ‌ۚ اَفَلَا تُبْصِرُوْنَؕ‏(51)\nWANAADAA FIRA’WNO FEE QAWMEHI QAALA LE-QAWMEHI A-LAYSA LEE MULKUS MESRA WA HAAZEHE ANHAARO TAJREE MIN TAHTEAA AFALAA TUBSEROONA.\nAnd Pharaoh proclaimed among his people, saying: “O my people! Does not the dominion of Egypt belong to me, (witness) these streams flowing underneath my (palace)? What! see ye not then? \nاَمْ اَنَا خَيْرٌ مِّنْ هٰذَا الَّذِىْ هُوَ مَهِيْنٌ ۙ وَّلَا يَكَادُ يُبِيْنُ‏(52)\nAM ANAA KHAYRUL MIN HAAZAA LAZEE HOWA MAHEENUN WA LAA YAKAADUL YUBEENU.\n“Am I not better than this (Moses), who is a contemptible wretch and can scarcely express himself clearly? \nفَلَوْلَاۤ اُلْقِىَ عَلَيْهِ اَسْوِرَةٌ مِّنْ ذَهَبٍ اَوْ جَآءَ مَعَهُ الْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ مُقْتَرِنِيْنَ‏(53)\nFA-LAWLAA ULQEYA A’LAYHE AASWERATUN MIN ZAHABIN AW JAAA-A MAA’AHU TAHMELOHUL MUQTARENEENA.\n“Then why are not gold bracelets bestowed on him, or (why) come (not) with him angels accompanying him in procession?” \nفَاسْتَخَفَّ قَوْمَهٗ فَاَطَاعُوْهُ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا قَوْمًا فٰسِقِيْنَ‏(54)\nFAASTAKHAFFA QAWMAH FAATAAU’OOHU INNAHUM KAANOO QAWMAN FAASEQEEN.\nThus did he make fools of his people, and they obeyed him: truly were they a people rebellious (against Allah). \nفَلَمَّاۤ اٰسَفُوْنَا انْتَقَمْنَا مِنْهُمْ فَاَغْرَقْنٰهُمْ اَجْمَعِيْنَۙ‏(55)\nFALAMMAA AAASAFOONAA ANTAQAMNAA MINHUM FAAGHRAQNAAHUM AJMA-E’ENA.\nWhen at length they provoked Us, We exacted retribution from them, and We drowned them all. \nفَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ سَلَفًا وَّمَثَلًا لِّلْاٰخِرِيْنَ‏(56)\nFAJAA’ALNAAHUM SALAFAN WWAMASALAN LLELAAAKHEREENA.\nAnd We made them (a people) of the Past and an Example to later ages. \nوَلَمَّا ضُرِبَ ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ مَثَلًا اِذَا قَوْمُكَ مِنْهُ يَصِدُّوْنَ‏(57)\nWA LAMMAA ZUREBA ABNU MARYAMAL MASALAA EZAA QAWMUKA MINHO YASEDDOONA.\nWhen (Jesus) the son of Mary is held up as an example, behold, thy people raise a clamour thereat (in ridicule)! \nوَقَالُوْٓا ءَاٰلِهَتُنَا خَيْرٌ اَمْ هُوَ‌ؕ مَا ضَرَبُوْهُ لَكَ اِلَّا جَدَلًا ؕ بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ خَصِمُوْنَ‏(58)\nWA A-TAJ-A’LO AALEHATUNAA KHAYRUL AM HOO MAA ZARABOOHU LAKA ILLAA JADALAN BAL HUM QAWMUN KHASEMOONA.\nAnd they say, “Are our gods best, or he?” This they set forth to thee, only by way of disputation: yea, they are a contentious people. \nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا عَبْدٌ اَنْعَمْنَا عَلَيْهِ وَجَعَلْنٰهُ مَثَلًا لِّبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَؕ‏(59)\nIN HOWA ILLAA A’ABDUN AN-A’MNAA A’LAYHE WA LAW MASALAA LLEBANEAA AESRAAEELA.\nHe was no more than a servant: We granted Our favour to him, and We made him an example to the Children of Israel. \nوَلَوْ نَشَآءُ لَجَعَلْنَا مِنْكُمْ مَّلٰٓئِكَةً فِى الْاَرْضِ يَخْلُفُوْنَ‏(60)\nWA LAW NASHAAA-O LAJAA’ALNAA MINKUM MMALAAAEKATAN FIL ARZE YAKHLUFOONA.\nAnd if it were Our Will, We could make angels from amongst you, succeeding each other on the earth. \nوَاِنَّهٗ لَعِلْمٌ لِّلسَّاعَةِ فَلَا تَمْتَرُنَّ بِهَا وَاتَّبِعُوْنِ‌ؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(61)\nWA INNAHU LAE’ELMUN LLELSSAAA’ATE FALAA TAMTARUNNA BEHAA WAATTABEU’OONE HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\nAnd (Jesus) shall be a Sign (for the coming of) the Hour (of Judgment): therefore have no doubt about the (Hour), but follow ye Me: this is a Straight Way. \nوَلَا يَصُدَّنَّكُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ‌ ۚ اِنَّهٗ لَكُمْ عَدُوٌّ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(62)\nWA LAA YASUDDANNAKUMU SHAYTAANO INNAHU LAKUM A’DUWWUM MOBEEN.\nLet not the Evil One hinder you: for he is to you an enemy avowed. \nوَ لَمَّا جَآءَ عِيْسٰى بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ قَالَ قَدْ جِئْتُكُمْ بِالْحِكْمَةِ وَلِاُبَيِّنَ لَكُمْ بَعْضَ الَّذِىْ تَخْتَلِفُوْنَ فِيْهِ‌ ۚ فَاتَّقُوا اللّٰهَ وَاَطِيْعُوْنِ‏(63)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A E’EESAA BIL-BAYYENAATE QAALA QAD JETUKUM BIL-HEKMATE WALEAUBAYNA LAKUM YAWM LAZEE TAKHTALEFOONA FEEHE FA TAQUL LAAHA WAATEEU’OONE.\nWhen Jesus came with Clear Signs, he said: “Now have I come to you with Wisdom, and in order to make clear to you some of the (points) on which ye dispute: therefore fear Allah and obey me. \nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ رَبِّىْ وَرَبُّكُمْ فَاعْبُدُوْهُ‌ؕ هٰذَا صِرَاطٌ مُّسْتَقِيْمٌ‏(64)\nINNAL LAAHA HOWA RABBEE WA RABBOKUM FAAA’BUDOOHU HAAZAA SERAATUM MUSTAQEEM.\n“For Allah, He is my Lord and your Lord: so worship ye Him: this is a Straight Way.” \nفَاخْتَلَفَ الْاَحْزَابُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِهِمْ‌ۚ فَوَيْلٌ لِّلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(65)\nFA TALAFA YAATIL MIN BAYNEHEM LAHUM LIL-LAZEENA ZALAMOO MIN A’ZAABIN YAWMIN ALEEM.\nBut sects from among themselves fell into disagreement: then woe to the wrong-doers, from the Penalty of a Grievous Day! \nهَلْ يَنْظُرُوْنَ اِلَّا السَّاعَةَ اَنْ تَاْتِيَهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(66)\nHAL YANZOROONA ILLAA SAA-A’TA AN TAATEEHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nDo they only wait for the Hour - that it should come on them all of a sudden, while they perceive not? \nاَلْاَخِلَّاۤءُ يَوْمَئِذٍۢ بَعْضُهُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ اِلَّا الْمُتَّقِيْنَ ؕ ‏(67)\nAALAAKHELLAAU YAWMA-EZIN KHALAA LE-BA’ZIN A’DUWWUM ILLAA MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nFriends on that day will be foes, one to another, except the Righteous. \nيٰعِبَادِ لَا خَوْفٌ عَلَيْكُمُ الْيَوْمَ وَلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ تَحْزَنُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(68)\nYAAE’EBAADE LAA KHAWFUN A’LAYKOMUL YAWMA WA LAA ANTUM TAHZANOONA.\nMy devotees! no fear shall be on you that Day, nor shall ye grieve, \nاَلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَكَانُوْا مُسْلِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(69)\nLAZEENA AAMANOO BE-AAYAATENAA WA KAANOO MUSLEMEEN.\n(Being) those who have believed in Our Signs and bowed (their wills to Ours) in Islam. \nاُدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ اَنْتُمْ وَاَزْوَاجُكُمْ تُحْبَرُوْنَ‌‏(70)\nAUDKHULOOA JANNATA ANTUM WAAZWAAJUKUM TUHBAROONA.\nEnter ye the Garden, ye and your wives, in (beauty and) rejoicing. \nيُطَافُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِصِحَافٍ مِّنْ ذَهَبٍ وَّاَكْوَابٍ‌ۚ وَفِيْهَا مَا تَشْتَهِيْهِ الْاَنْفُسُ وَتَلَذُّ الْاَعْيُنُ‌ۚ وَاَنْتُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(71)\nYUTAAFU A’LAYHIM BESEHAAFIN MIN ZAHABIN WA AKWAABIN WA FEEHAA MAA TASHTAHEEHE AL-AANFUSU WATALAZZU AL-AAA’YUNU WA ANTUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nTo them will be passed round, dishes and goblets of gold: there will be there all that the souls could desire, all that their ayes could delight in: and ye shall abide therein (for eye). \nوَتِلْكَ الْجَنَّةُ الَّتِىْۤ اُوْرِثْتُمُوْهَا بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(72)\nWA TILKAL JANNATO LATEE AOORESTUMOOHAA BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nSuch will be the Garden of which ye are made heirs for your (good) deeds (in life). \nلَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَاكِهَةٌ كَثِيْرَةٌ مِّنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ‏(73)\nLAKUM FEEHAA FAAKEHATUNW KASEERATUN MINHAA TAAKULOONA.\nYe shall have therein abundance of fruit, from which ye shall have satisfaction. \nاِنَّ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ فِىْ عَذَابِ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدُوْنَ ۚ ۖ‏(74)\nINNAL MUJREMEEN FEE A’ZAABIN JAHANNAMA KHAALEDOON.\nThe sinners will be in the Punishment of Hell, to dwell therein (for aye): \nلَا يُفَتَّرُ عَنْهُمْ وَهُمْ فِيْهِ مُبْلِسُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(75)\nLAA YUFATTARU A’NHUM WA HUM FEEHE MUBLESOONA.\nNowise will the (Punishment) be lightened for them, and in despair will they be there overwhelmed. \nوَمَا ظَلَمْنٰهُمْ وَ لٰكِنْ كَانُوْا هُمُ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(76)\nWA MAA ZALAMNAAHUM WA LAAKEN KAANOO HOMUL ZAALEMEEN.\nNowise shall We be unjust to them: but it is they who have been unjust themselves. \nوَنَادَوْا يٰمٰلِكُ لِيَقْضِ عَلَيْنَا رَبُّكَ‌ؕ قَالَ اِنَّكُمْ مّٰكِثُوْنَ‏(77)\nWANAADAWA YAAMAALEKU LE-YAQZE A’LAYNAA RABBUKA QAALA INNAKUM MMAAKESOONA.\nThey will cry: “O Malik! would that thy Lord put an end to us!” He will say, “Nay, but ye shall abide!” \nلَقَدْ جِئْنٰكُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَكُمْ لِلْحَقِّ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(78)\nLAQAD JENAAKUM BIL-HAQQE LAAKINNAL AAKSARAKUM LIL-HAQQE KAAREHOONA.\nVerily We have brought the Truth to you: but most of you have a hatred for Truth. \nاَمْ اَبْرَمُوْۤا اَمْرًا فَاِنَّا مُبْرِمُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(79)\nAM AABRAMOOA AMRAN FAINNAA MUBREMOONA.\nWhat! have they settled some plan (among themselves)? But it is We Who settle things. \nاَمْ يَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّا لَا نَسْمَعُ سِرَّهُمْ وَنَجْوٰٮهُمْ‌ؕ بَلٰى وَرُسُلُنَا لَدَيْهِمْ يَكْتُبُوْنَ‏(80)\nAM YAHSABOONAL ANNAA LAA NASMA-O SERRAHUM WANAJWAAHUM BALAA WA ROSOLONAA LADAYHIM YAKTOBOONAL.\nOr do they think that We hear not their secrets and their private counsels? Indeed (We do), and Our messengers are by them, to record. \nقُلْ اِنْ كَانَ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ وَلَدٌۖ فَاَنَا اَوَّلُ الْعٰبِدِيْنَ‏(81)\nQUL IN KAANA LELRRAHMAANE WALADUN FA ANAA AAWLU AL-A’AABEDEENA.\nSay: “If (Allah) Most Gracious had a son, I would be the first to worship.” \nسُبْحٰنَ رَبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ رَبِّ الْعَرْشِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(82)\nLAAHE RABBE SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE RABBE A’RSHIL A’MMAA YASEFOONA.\nGlory to the Lord of the heavens and the earth, the Lord of the Throne (of Authority)! (He is free) from the things they attribute (to him)! \nفَذَرْهُمْ يَخُوْضُوْا وَيَلْعَبُوْا حَتّٰى يُلٰقُوْا يَوْمَهُمُ الَّذِىْ يُوْعَدُوْنَ‏(83)\nFAZARHUM YAKHOOZOOA WAYALA’ABOOA HATTAA YULAAQOOA YAWMAHUMU LAZEE YOOA’ADOONA.\nSo leave them to babble and play (with vanities) until they meet that Day of theirs, which they have been promised. \nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ فِى السَّمَآءِ اِلٰهٌ وَّفِى الْاَرْضِ اِلٰهٌ‌ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(84)\nWA HOWA LAZEE FIL SAMAAA-E ELAAHUN WA FIL ARZE ELAAHUN WA HOWA HAKEEM A’LEEM.\nIt is He Who is Allah in heaven and Allah on earth; and He is full of Wisdom and Knowledge. \nوَتَبٰرَكَ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا‌ ۚ وَعِنْدَهٗ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ‌ ۚ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(85)\nWA TABAARAKAS-MO LAZEE LAHU MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA I’NDAHU I’LMUS AS-SAAA’ATE WA ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nAnd blessed is He to Whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and all between them: with Him is the Knowledge of the Hour (of Judgment): and to Him shall ye be brought back. \nوَلَا يَمْلِكُ الَّذِيْنَ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهِ الشَّفَاعَةَ اِلَّا مَنْ شَهِدَ بِالْحَقِّ وَهُمْ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(86)\nWA LAA YAMLEKU LAZEENA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHE ASH-SHAFAAA’ATA ILLAA MAN SHAHEDA BIL-HAQQE WA HUM YA’LAMOON.\nAnd those whom they invoke besides Allah have no power of intercession;- only he who bears witness to the Truth, and they know (him). \nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَهُمْ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ فَاَنّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَۙ‏(87)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM MAN KHALAQAHUM LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAHO FA-ANNAA YOAFEKOON.\nIf thou ask them, who created them, they will certainly say, Allah: How then are they deluded away (from the Truth)? \nوَقِيْلِهٖ يٰرَبِّ اِنَّ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ قَوْمٌ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‌ۘ‏(88)\nWAQEELEH YAA RABBE INNAL HAAOOLAAA-E QAWMUN LAA YOAMENOONA.\n(Allah has knowledge) of the (Prophet's) cry, “O my Lord! Truly these are people who will not believe!” \nفَاصْفَحْ عَنْهُمْ وَقُلْ سَلٰمٌ‌ؕ فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(89)\nFAASFAH A’NHUM WA QUL SALAAMUN FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\nBut turn away from them, and say “Peace!” But soon shall they know! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Zukhruf (The Embellishment)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 89 verses. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah will be saved from the vermin (e.g. insects, scorpions etc.) in the grave and will not undergo the squeezing in the grave.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that drinking water in which this Surah was dissolved acts as a cure and a relief from pain."
